# riffle/

Test suite covering architectural layer separation, state mutation invariants, and integration across the predicate engine, pattern layer, and service. Enforces the Highlander principle through boundary fences (waist-engine separation, pattern layer isolation), single-transition guarantee (context updates), and absence of silent failures.

## Dirs

- `cli/` -- CLI command handlers and configuration tests
- `ctx/` -- Context module and state machine behavior tests
- `docs/` -- Documentation and specification tests
- `predicate/` -- Predicate engine evaluation, DSL resolution, and standard library tests
- `service/` -- Service layer CSV processing, pipeline execution, and error handling tests
- `sia/` -- Sia pattern layer staging, pipeline sourcing, and result consistency tests

## Files

- `boundary_fence_test.exs` -- Architectural fence: waist and engine layers name only authorized modules; pattern layer is named by none of them
- `extrication_gate_test.exs` -- Invariant: no source-project trace strings in compiled artifacts
- `single_transition_fence_test.exs` -- Fence: Ctx struct updates occur only in waist; Invariant: pattern layer performs no map mutations
